dip declined Halifax even though it says debt completed. Um,</p><p>Megan Gordon: Well had debt has been completed technically and it isn&#x27;t a claim. Yeah.</p><p>Bob Duncan: So, what&#x27;s happening with that case then? I&#x27;ll leave you guys to debate that.</p><p>Megan Gordon: We spoke about it this morning. Karen&#x27;s going to look at it.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Okay, nice find completed tracking contact appointment booked. That&#x27;s, what I want to do is I want to look at.</p><p>Karen Lochhead: The if Halifax is kind of. So this is the one we&#x27;re trying to get an offer accepted for with Siobhan Rice, she&#x27;s actually lovely but she her husband&#x27;s been a contract has been employed for, The same job, right? But has now because when Rolls Royce take you on, they take you on as a contract first, right? So now he&#x27;s a contractor with six months. Would I be better off checking his payslip because it mightn&#x27;t say contractor? Yeah,</p><p>Bob Duncan: That&#x27;s what I would do.</p><p>Karen Lochhead: Yeah, I kind of feel that. What&#x27;d you say? Yeah. Technically like yeah.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Technically not technically about it It&#x27;s 100%. Anyway, um, There&#x27;s a few here that created. So I&#x27;m not quite sure what&#x27;s going on because that looks like that has been booked in. This is down. This is a member of staff that you&#x27;ve just got as created. So I don&#x27;t know who created that.</p><p>Karen Lochhead: Don&#x27;t know who is he? Jenna Deacon Oh Jenna Deacon That&#x27;s that space or she&#x27;s actually left now by the way, That and go Um.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Well, there&#x27;s a few in here that we probably need to tidy up. Then yeah So I. Think on the leads front. Leads are probably starting to pick up, but we I know you need more. The conversation will probably happen with Craig today, tomorrow, and then the conversation happened with Maitland and Lewis next week. And then from then there&#x27;ll be a bit of an introduction.