I&#x27;m just so why is your written business? Not as high as it as what I was expecting it to be? Then?</p><p>Karen Lochhead: Well, because I still have four reports to do five reports.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Because you don&#x27;t think your written went up this week. Has it? Um half of them on.</p><p>Megan Gordon: Our list of suitabilities are still to be added, like product be added,</p><p>Bob Duncan: Right? Okay.</p><p>Karen Lochhead: So I&#x27;ve done three and I have about six to do, right?</p><p>Bob Duncan: And have you secured the products?</p><p>Megan Gordon: Yeah, yeah. Yeah, because the apps are done. She&#x27;s just not done Midas.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Right, okay. So it&#x27;s getting onto Midas then. So could you just put your finger out Caroline and get that done? If I wasn&#x27;t running these meetings,</p><p>Karen Lochhead: This would be doing that.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Well thing is, if you just did it, then we wouldn&#x27;t have these meetings with you. Okay fair enough, You know catch her, too. Yeah. Um. Right, so Leeds business written. So, it looks like you&#x27;re probably going to have quite a strong business written month, then as it stands right now with everything that&#x27;s sitting there. Yeah, I mean if you put a number roughly on that, what would that be Karen?</p><p>Karen Lochhead: I think I think there&#x27;s about 10, 000 pounds worth of business there. By the way, definitely because a lot of them have fees, right? Mhm. So I&#x27;ve started to do my fee situations again right and yeah. And there&#x27;s protection there, so so that so I put on one protection. Yes, it was only thirty pounds. I am chasing her right and Sean has good protection. That&#x27;s about sixty pounds right Marty and thing is about ninety poundsum, so those protections are all right.</p><p>Bob Duncan: It&#x27;s about four grand there yeah.</p><p>Karen Lochhead: The mortgages are a bit decent right, So some of t here is two that are about five hundred under five hundred th